bar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"506c8fe4d1115946ec22e241f816d3dc7b63405aa6fbf6564ee62341a14ce4fe","event_uuid":"fca7a0f9-f190-404f-9bd2-e7dfd2116a14","position":{"commit_sha":"484f504c1b98f19c06e95771ed1a312d491e55be","position":"1786565267305689240-fca7a0f9-f190-404f-9bd2-e7dfd2116a14"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e8096cd895134da7149052922a9f32fb9307079a672c1d8719107e366a9a6851","event_uuid":"607e191a-a56b-4892-9075-9054edbcae40","position":{"commit_sha":"95ea4238173e2a08fa30933807e8c4fd4982846a","position":"1786567951824258023-607e191a-a56b-4892-9075-9054edbcae40"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in worktree ../despotic-s1 (branch despotic-s1);\npushed as Gerrit change 1672 (commit 98ef247339, rebar-ticket trailer 248f-ac00-18db-4259).\n\n## What landed\n\n- NEW `peer_confirmations.py` (187 LOC): `PeerConfirmationStore` +\n  `record_key(source, target, relation)` + `open_store(repo_root)`, SCHEMA_VERSION 1, atomic\n  mkstemp/os.replace save, fail-OPEN load (corrupt or absent -> empty, never raises).\n- `dispatch_one.py`: `update_one` and `_update_one_dispatch_links` gain an optional\n  `link_confirm` keyword; `set_relationship`'s return value (previously discarded) is captured\n  so `result[\"id\"]` can be recorded as the vendor link id.\n- `dispatch_apply_phases.py`: `_confirm_link_add` — the swallow-everything invocation wrapper.\n- `apply_handlers.py`: `_make_link_confirm` builds the sink from `BatchApplyContext`\n  (`binding_store`, `pass_id`, `repo_root`) and `handle_update` passes it into `update_one`.\n- `git_adapter.py`: `PEER_CONFIRMATIONS_FILE` + `__all__` export.\n- `reconcile_helpers.py`: staged in BOTH `_rel_files` AND `_tracked_basenames`.\n\n## Three plan corrections the plan-review gate caught (all verified against the code first)\n\n1. Staging in `_rel_files` alone is INSUFFICIENT: `_commit_binding_store_snapshot` keeps a\n   second parallel `_tracked_basenames` set (the bug-1e08 per-file idempotency guard) and\n   returns \"already up-to-date\" when no tracked basename is staged, silently dropping a\n   confirmation-only change on every pass.\n2. The original plan's \"no key translation is needed\" was WRONG — the outbound ADD entry carries\n   Jira keys (`to_key`), not local ids, so the target needs `get_local_id` reverse-mapping and\n   an unbound target must record nothing rather than persist a vendor key in a local-id field.\n3. The write site was targeted at `apply_outbound._apply_outbound_update`, which is NOT the\n   production outbound-update path — production dispatches through `apply_handlers.handle_update`,\n   so the callback would never have fired in production. Rebuilt there instead, where\n   `BatchApplyContext` already carries everything needed (no new plumbing).\n\n## Module-size note\n\nAdding the helper inline pushed `dispatch_one.py` to 805 lines, OVER the 800 hard cap. Resolved\nby moving `_confirm_link_add` to the established sibling leaf `dispatch_apply_phases.py` (the\nsame seam ticket 744a/a3fa used for exactly this reason). Final sizes: dispatch_one 786,\ndispatch_apply_phases 416, apply_handlers 460, peer_confirmations 187, reconcile_helpers 675,\ngit_adapter 302 — all under 800.\n\n## Verification (worktree venv)\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py` -> 20 passed\n- `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` -> 2421 passed (no regression)\n- `make lint` -> exit 0; `make typecheck` -> Success, 510 source files\n- MUTATION CHECK: removing `os.path.basename(git_adapter.PEER_CONFIRMATIONS_FILE)` from\n  `_tracked_basenames` turns `test_commit_only_peer_confirmations_is_staged_and_committed` RED\n  (\"confirmation-only change was not committed\"); restoring it turns it GREEN. The test pins the\n  bug-1e08 trap itself, not the diff.\n\nAwaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before close.","timestamp":1786562143954410001}],"created_at":1786558444278129001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6b81f526-5af0-43c1-b44e-5472e7543e83","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7873-ef2f-a527-45f7"},{"link_uuid":"fca7a0f9-f190-404f-9bd2-e7dfd2116a14","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0407-1796-5305-41b9"},{"link_uuid":"607e191a-a56b-4892-9075-9054edbcae40","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ffd4-2947-b807-4d4e"}],"description":"## Context\n\nParent epic `a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb`. `managed_refs` (`src/rebar/reducer/_managed_refs.py`) marks a\nref managed the instant it is created LOCALLY and is strictly monotonic, so guard G3 in the\ninbound removal path cannot tell a never-pushed local link from a peer-deleted one. This story\nadds the missing evidence store; it changes NO removal behavior (S3 does that). The record is a\nFULL record (vendor link id, direction, confirming pass, confirmed-at), not a boolean — see the\nepic's \"Chosen direction\" and its comment \"Decomposition design calls\" (D1 storage home, D2 key\nshape, D3 pass_id).\n\n## Scope\n\nNew module `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/peer_confirmations.py`, modelled on the sidecar\n`impossible_links.py` (SCHEMA_VERSION, store-relative path, atomic mkstemp + `os.replace` save).\n\n- Store file: `.tickets-tracker/.bridge_state/peer_confirmations.json`.\n- Record key: `(source_local_id, target_local_id, relation)` — LOCAL ids, relation-scoped,\n  matching `_inbound_unlink_one` (relation-scoped since e39f) and `impossible_links.record_key`.\n- Record fields: `link_id`, `direction` (`outbound` | `snapshot`), `confirmed_pass`,\n  `confirmed_at` (epoch ns), `source` (`push` | `snapshot` | `backfill`).\n- API: `open_store(repo_root)`, `is_confirmed(source, target, relation)`,\n  `record(source, target, relation, *, link_id, direction, pass_id, source_kind)`, `save()`.\n\n**Write seam (three edits, callback-shaped).** The success point is\n`dispatch_one.py::_update_one_dispatch_links` at the `set_relationship` call, but that function\nhas neither a binding store nor a pass id and must not gain knowledge of either:\n\n1. `dispatch_one.py` — `update_one(...)` and `_update_one_dispatch_links(...)` each gain an\n   optional keyword `link_confirm: Callable[..., None] | None = None`; the sole internal call\n   site (`dispatch_one.py:454`) forwards it. `None` preserves today's behavior byte-for-byte.\n   After `set_relationship` returns, invoke `link_confirm(to_key=..., relation=..., link_id=...)`.\n   The call is inside the existing `try`, AFTER `_links_applied += 1`, so a failed\n   `set_relationship` records nothing. The invocation is itself wrapped so that ANY exception\n   from the callback (`record()` / `save()`) is logged to stderr and swallowed — a confirmation\n   write must never fail an outbound link that already landed, and must never perturb the\n   counters.\n2. `dispatch_one.py` — capture `set_relationship`'s return value (typed `dict[str, Any]` in\n   `_backend.py::SupportsLinks`, currently discarded) and pass `result.get(\"id\")` as `link_id`\n   when the return is a Mapping, else `None`. Backends may legitimately return no id; a missing\n   id is recorded as `null` and is NOT a failure.\n3. `apply_handlers.py::handle_update` — build the callback and pass it into the `update_one(...)`\n   call at line 211. This is the PRODUCTION outbound-update path, and its `BatchApplyContext`\n   already holds `client`, `repo_root`, `pass_id` and `binding_store`, so no new plumbing is\n   needed (the same context-to-dispatch pattern `synced_fields` already uses). The callback\n   translates keys to the record shape: source is `mutation[\"local_id\"]`, target is\n   `ctx.binding_store.get_local_id(to_key)`. **When the reverse map returns None the target is\n   unbound — skip recording entirely** (never persist a Jira key in a local-id field); the\n   confirmation is picked up next pass, or by S2 from a snapshot. `apply_outbound.py`'s typed\n   leaf is deliberately NOT edited: it delegates to the same `update_one` and passing no\n   callback leaves it exactly as today.\n\n**Durability — three edits, not one.** Adding the path to `_rel_files` alone is insufficient:\n`reconcile_helpers.py::_commit_binding_store_snapshot` builds a SECOND, parallel\n`_tracked_basenames` set (the bug-1e08 per-file idempotency guard) and returns \"already\nup-to-date\" when no tracked basename is staged, so a confirmation-only change would be dropped.\n\n1. `git_adapter.py` — add `PEER_CONFIRMATIONS_FILE = f\"{BRIDGE_STATE_DIR}/peer_confirmations.json\"`\n   and export it in `__all__`.\n2. `reconcile_helpers.py` — append it to `_rel_files`.\n3. `reconcile_helpers.py` — append its basename to `_tracked_basenames`.\n\nLoad/save is fail-OPEN (like `bindings-retired.json`, NOT fail-closed like `bindings.json`): a\ncorrupt or absent store degrades to \"nothing confirmed\" without aborting the pass. S4 supplies\nthe backfill that makes \"nothing confirmed\" safe.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 `peer_confirmations.py` has a `SCHEMA_VERSION` constant and is under 400 LOC; every\n      edited module stays under the 800-line cap. Proof: `bash -c 'git archive HEAD | tar -xO\n      src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py | wc -l'` per edited file, each < 800.\n- [ ] AC2 `record()` then `is_confirmed()` is True for exactly that `(source, target, relation)`\n      and False for the same pair under a different relation. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py -k relation_scoped`.\n- [ ] AC3 A successful outbound ADD through `_update_one_dispatch_links` invokes `link_confirm`\n      and writes a record with `direction=\"outbound\"`, `source=\"push\"`, the dispatched relation\n      and the `pass_id`; a `set_relationship` that raises writes NO record. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py -k dispatch`.\n- [ ] AC4 `link_id` is taken from `set_relationship`'s returned mapping (`result[\"id\"]`) and is\n      `null` when the backend returns no id or a non-mapping — neither case is an error. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py -k link_id`.\n- [ ] AC5 An unbound target (`binding_store.get_local_id(to_key)` returns None) records NOTHING\n      and does not raise. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py -k unbound`.\n- [ ] AC6 With `link_confirm=None`, `_links_computed` / `_links_applied` are identical to\n      pre-change behavior on the success, failure and dedup-skip paths. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py -k counter`.\n- [ ] AC7 The store survives a ticket-log SNAPSHOT compaction (confirm, compact, re-open, still\n      confirmed). Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py -k compaction`.\n- [ ] AC8 A corrupt or absent `peer_confirmations.json` yields an empty store and does NOT raise.\n      Proof: `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py -k corrupt`.\n- [ ] AC9 `_commit_binding_store_snapshot` COMMITS when `peer_confirmations.json` is the ONLY\n      changed file (proves both `_rel_files` and `_tracked_basenames` were updated). Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py -k commit_only`.\n- [ ] AC10 A `link_confirm` callback that RAISES is logged and swallowed: the outbound link\n      still counts as applied and `_links_applied` is unchanged. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py -k callback_raises`.\n- [ ] AC11 Gates green. Proof: `make lint` exit 0, `make typecheck` exit 0,\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` exit 0.\n\n## Testing\n\n- New suite `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py` covering store\n  round-trip, relation scoping, corrupt/absent load, compaction survival, the dispatch write\n  point (success, raise, dedup-skip), `link_id` extraction, the unbound-target skip, a raising\n  callback, counter parity under `link_confirm=None`, and the commit-when-only-changed-file case.\n- Regression: `make lint && make typecheck && pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` — this story is\n  additive and must not alter existing dispatch or removal behavior.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nSnapshot-sourced confirmation (S2), the removal decline (S3), backfill (S4).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/peer_confirmations.py","reason":"NEW: peer-confirmation record store (schema, key, load/record/save)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"optional link_confirm callback; capture set_relationship return for link_id"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"build the link_confirm callback from BatchApplyContext in handle_update"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"stage the sidecar in _rel_files AND _tracked_basenames (bug-1e08 guard)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/git_adapter.py","reason":"PEER_CONFIRMATIONS_FILE constant + __all__ export"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py","reason":"NEW: store, dispatch write, counter parity, compaction, commit-only-file"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb"],["relates_to","0407-1796-5305-41b9"],["relates_to","7873-ef2f-a527-45f7"],["relates_to","ffd4-2947-b807-4d4e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb","parent_status_uuid":"97515ee3-e833-47c8-a91f-dd6700a54761","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"248f-ac00-18db-4259","ticket_type":"story","title":"Persist a peer-confirmation record per managed link","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1be1985b-cbae-4ea0-8237-3bca6ab61887","d8d52953-7189-438c-8f20-09cdd0e74da0","4ad7208a-3b9d-47c4-bc7f-43a9a3a071c1","8f116f58-088a-4c67-96d4-aea9d240eef4","4f7183b8-a7dd-452a-846c-00b19c85a751","c8346df4-2391-44c6-a8aa-e158252aa2f4","507e077f-45a1-46b9-ac07-07089909f7ad","881e13ef-fd18-4c7c-87f0-fe826f9ad210","97515ee3-e833-47c8-a91f-dd6700a54761","2e0bb8cc-b7eb-4d1a-8f84-7de44b2c1a6c","8c45932c-de64-4d75-af5b-6e3963d66c19","6b81f526-5af0-43c1-b44e-5472e7543e83","fca7a0f9-f190-404f-9bd2-e7dfd2116a14","607e191a-a56b-4892-9075-9054edbcae40"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786567951824258024,"uuid":"27fa3f11-bcc9-40bc-b922-60c905ba1b82"}